Think: Process each path from temp_workspace/file_list.csv: count lines per file, output "full_path,line_count" to temp_workspace/per_file_line_counts.csv, and record any read errors to temp_workspace/errors.log. I'll run a single awk command that reads file_list.csv, attempts to getline from each path to count lines, prints counts to stdout (redirected to per_file_line_counts.csv), and writes errors at END to errors.log.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -F, '{
 path=$1;
 n=0;
 status = getline line < path;
 if (status < 0) { errors[path]=1; next }
 if (status > 0) { n=1; while ((getline line < path) > 0) n++; }
 close(path);
 print path","n
}
END {
 for (e in errors) print e >> "temp_workspace/errors.log"
}' temp_workspace/file_list.csv > temp_workspace/per_file_line_counts.csv
```

