Think: Create the script file temp_log_count/count_var_log_kb.sh containing a single command (an awk invocation) that reads the file list and writes the integer kilobyte total to stdout and to total_kb.txt. Use the recorded absolute workspace path from temp_log_count/workspace_path.txt when embedding paths.

Act: bash

```bash
cat > temp_log_count/count_var_log_kb.sh <<EOF
#!/bin/sh
awk -v out="$(cat temp_log_count/workspace_path.txt)/total_kb.txt" '
BEGIN { total = 0; }
{
  # build a stat command to get file size in bytes, suppress stat errors
  cmd = "stat -c %s -- \"" $0 "\" 2>/dev/null";
  if ((cmd | getline size) <= 0) {
    print "Warning: cannot read " $0 > "/dev/stderr";
    close(cmd);
    next;
  }
  close(cmd);
  # convert bytes to kilobytes using integer arithmetic (round up)
  kb = int((size + 1023) / 1024);
  total += kb;
}
END {
  # write integer total to the output file and to stdout
  printf "%d\n", total > out;
  print total;
}' "$(cat temp_log_count/workspace_path.txt)/file_list.txt"
EOF
```

